     <h1 class="title" title="Panhala Hill Station">Panhala</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">
<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/west-india-hill-stations/panhala-hill-station.jpg" title="Panhala hill station" alt="Panhala hill station, hill stations in india, west india hill stations, Panhala" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location: Kolhapur, Maharashtra</b>.<br />
<b>Significance: The Golden Peak</b><br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 977m above sea level<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 25&#176;C - 32&#176;C, Winter 15&#176;C - 20&#176;C<br />
<b>Best time to visit:</b> October to June</p>     
<p>Almost all travel packages to include a <b>trip to Panhala</b> . The <b>Ambarkhana</b> was built by the Marathas and is home to the palace, the administrative department and in the barn. The granaries were necessary as the need to store grain in case of famine and other calamities. You can also take a look at <b>Teen Darwaja</b>, there are three doors, giving access to the fort.</p>
